  "comments": "House of Windsor (1917 to date), Elizabeth II (1952-2022), Pre-decimal issues (1953-70).<br /><br />\r\nThe standard weight of these coins was 105 grains.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse die varieties:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Obv 1</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(Set issue)</span> I of LIZ further from corner, corner to one side of H of BETH, shallow portrait;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Obv 2</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(Circulation)</span> I of LIZ closer to corner, corner more central to H of BETH, recut portrait;<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6044fe0b0b0bf.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6044fe0b0b0bf.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\nImage above is reproduced with kind permission of Declan Magee and Numista member Sjoelund.<br /><br />\r\nA special mint set was released comprising 2s. 6d. to 1/4d. ordinary business strikes in transparent envelopes (1,288,000 issued).<br /><br />\r\nAlso, a special proof set was released comprising 5s. to 1/4d. struck from polished dies and sold in special cases (40,000 issued).",
